Reason: Chromium mutes a tab by closing its audio output streams and opening
fake ones, and unmutes by swapping back. Video playback follows the audio
clock, so a playing video froze or skipped a frame each time the app's
Audio panel muted or unmuted the page (November 1, 2026). A muted stream now
keeps playing at volume 0 (OutputController::OutputVolume); loopback capture
still gets the audio at the page's volume, as before. Upstream main swaps
streams the same way. No upstream bug.

